The spoken movement can be summarized as $\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{Clarity}
&\Rightarrow \mathrm{No\ Choice}
\Rightarrow \mathrm{Action}, \\
\mathrm{Choice}
&\Rightarrow \mathrm{Confusion}
\Rightarrow \mathrm{Resistance/Conflict}.\end{aligned}$ The notation should remain subordinate to the statement. The point is not that all practical selection is confused. The point is that inward choice, as the lecture uses the word, belongs to a divided mind.

