p.src:
A short derivation keeps the sequence clear: $\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{Pleasure\ as\ image}
&\Rightarrow \mathrm{Dependence}, \\
\mathrm{Dependence}
&\Rightarrow \mathrm{Fear}, \\
\mathrm{Pleasure\ as\ image}
&\Rightarrow \mathrm{Fear}.\end{aligned}$ This is a worked logical chain, not a psychological theory added from outside. It follows the lecture’s order: thought sustains pleasure, pleasure carries dependence, dependence contains fear, and what contains fear cannot be love.

